From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: enable binfmt_misc for foreign executables

gmux runs x86-64 and AArch64 ELF binaries through katybug, a wasm user
program that translates them. binfmt_misc lets execve() of such a file
start the registered interpreter with the file's path, so the process
keeps its own argv, credentials and file descriptors and needs nothing
from the host. The rootfs registers the two ELF machine types at boot.
---
--- a/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig
+++ b/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ CONFIG_EXPERT=y
 CONFIG_HVC_WASM=y
 # CONFIG_COMPAT_32BIT_TIME is not set
 CONFIG_BINFMT_WASM=y
+CONFIG_BINFMT_MISC=y
 # CONFIG_COREDUMP is not set
 # CONFIG_COMPAT_BRK is not set
 # CONFIG_VM_EVENT_COUNTERS is not set
